🌟 Goal:
Create a project-specific dev workflow file (`/ai/instructions/dev_workflow.mdc`) for the beauty salon site. 
This will define how we structure development, commits, QA, i18n, booking integration, and TaskMaster usage.

🤩 Input:
- Tech stack: Next.js (App Router, TS), Tailwind, shadcn/ui, framer-motion, next-intl, next-seo, Resend
- Booking integration: Trafft (multi-master, deposits, cancellations)
- AI tools: Cursor + TaskMaster (MCP/CLI hybrid model)
- Target outcome: clean workflow, task-driven structure, low-friction QA

☑ Must:
- Define 2 modes of operation (MCP server as default, CLI as fallback)
- Include step-by-step workflow (init → parse PRD → expand → implement → log → commit → QA)
- Specify task structure (id, title, status, priority, dependencies, subtasks)
- Cover logging & drift correction (update_subtask, update_task)
- Booking-specific QA rules (policies shown, iframe loads, i18n working)
- Status codes table (pending, in-progress, done, deferred)
- Git commit convention (e.g., feat:/fix:/chore:)
- Reference linked instruction files (`@cursor_rules.mdc`, `@ui_styleguide.mdc`)
- Mark as alwaysApply: false

🚫 Avoid:
- Overly generic “ClickRevamp” context (make it salon-appropriate)
- Duplicating styleguide rules (only workflow/QA here)
- Long-winded history of TaskMaster (keep actionable)
